# Slice 1+2+3 (Layer A density v1) fixture: 21-fixpoint-factorial
# rewritten to use the full v1 stack.
#
# Slice 1 — implicit prelude: no PRM Int/Bool, no FNT/FN for sub/mul/eqInt
#   (they all resolve to reserved synthetic nodes).
# Slice 2 — inline literals: `0`, `1`, `5` appear directly in arg lists
#   instead of `zero ILT 0`, `one ILT 1`, `five ILT 5`. `true` and `false`
#   appear directly in MC patterns (via PLT slot).
# Slice 3 — auto-VarRef: `n` and `recurse` appear as bare PRC binder
#   references in arg lists; the emitter synthesizes VarRefs implicitly.
#
# Round-trip property: canonical root hash equals 21-fixpoint-factorial.json's.
# Compressed from 34 lines (890 bytes) explicit form to 16 lines:
# bigger savings come in v1.5 (IF sugar) and v2 (more sugar).
@v=1 root=app
factT FNT [intT] intT
recurse PRC "recurse" factT
n PRC "n" intT
nIsZero APP eqInt [n 0]
litTrue BLT true
patTrue PLT boolT litTrue
caseTrue MC patTrue 1
litFalse BLT false
patFalse PLT boolT litFalse
nMinus1 APP sub [n 1]
recCall APP recurse [nMinus1]
mulBody APP mul [n recCall]
caseFalse MC patFalse mulBody
matchBody MAT nIsZero [caseTrue caseFalse]
bodyLam LAM [recurse n] matchBody
fact FIX factT bodyLam
app APP fact [5]
